  Source revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>. All
  manuscript files remain drafts. Bounded agent passes are recorded
  separately in <verbatim|reviews/draft-review.md>; they do not set the
  unit's independent review fields.

  The source root abbreviated below is <verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/RG_NEXT_COMPLETE_REPEATABLE_NONLINEAR_STEP/>.
  Declarations below have namespace <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat> unless
  specified.

  <section|Numerical and healthy-boundary
  estimates><label|numerical-and-healthy-boundary-estimates>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|healthy-boundary-jets.tex>: <verbatim|Boulevard.Oro>
    chart conversion and radial retreat; <verbatim|Boulevard.Term> summable
    derivative passage; <verbatim|Boulevard.Ebb> and
    <verbatim|Boulevard.Views> centered healthy-boundary extension. Paths:
    <verbatim|Boulevard/{Oro,Term,Ebb,Views}.lean>. <verbatim|Sienna.vow>,
    <verbatim|Sienna.eaves>, <verbatim|Sienna.furl> in
    <verbatim|Sienna/Nuts.lean> fix -7/16 and -1. The chart bound is on the
    centered function throughout a common strict-health neighborhood;
    extension differentiates the globally regular action, not a hard cutoff.

    <item><verbatim|small-field-budget-selection.tex>:
    <verbatim|Meadow.rain/spur>, <verbatim|Meadow.flights/extraHeight>,
    <verbatim|Boulevard.Dawn>, <verbatim|Trio.Ninety>,
    <verbatim|Roof.compar/dishes/ensures>,
    <verbatim|Marlin.pennies/bound_up/pricingBuy>. Source files
    <verbatim|Meadow/Equip.lean>, <verbatim|Meadow/Storeys.lean>,
    <verbatim|Boulevard/Dawn.lean>, <verbatim|Trio/Ninety.lean>,
    <verbatim|Roof/Porch.lean>, <verbatim|Marlin/Slots.lean>. These are
    numerical consequences of supplied activity prices. The actual auxiliary
    suppliers and incoming funded history are separate obligations.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Truncated integral and full pure
  logarithm><label|truncated-integral-and-full-pure-logarithm>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|truncated-stationary-log.tex>: <verbatim|Lantern.Golf>,
    <verbatim|Lantern.ratify>, <verbatim|Lantern.lookingGlass> and the
    interpolation/Gaussian-tail helpers, inspected in
    <verbatim|Lantern/{Port,Mesh,Predict,Spat,Blips,Lens}.lean>. The integral
    at b=0 remains a truncated Gaussian mass; symmetry is b -\<gtr\> -b with
    z -\<gtr\> -z. The moving Hessian determinant is retained. Order
    purchases and the monitor's stronger growth properties are explicit.

    <item><verbatim|pure-action-small-field.tex>: <verbatim|Token.languid> in
    <verbatim|Token/Purple.lean>, with relative positive-kernel derivative
    estimates in <verbatim|Token/{Fluent,Card,Trebles}.lean>;
    <verbatim|Shellac.erudite> in <verbatim|Shellac/Sables.lean>,
    <verbatim|Shellac.pole> in <verbatim|Shellac/Mars.lean>, and
    <verbatim|Shellac.auster> in <verbatim|Shellac/Smug.lean> plus
    <verbatim|Shellac/Proof.lean> and <verbatim|Shellac/Turmeric.lean>. The
    exact signs agree with <verbatim|Fare.coverLog> in
    <verbatim|Fare/Bingo.lean>. Fixed-stage quadratic matching is a retained
    input.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Actual exterior receipt><label|actual-exterior-receipt>

  <verbatim|stationary-exterior-receipt.tex> follows the actual
  <verbatim|Sienna.reaches> route:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|Fare.actU/overall/amt/staying/cubits>
    (<verbatim|Fare/Sum.lean>): tree-gauge probability integral, compact
    retained region, exact Haar/affine change.

    <item><verbatim|Fare.coverLog/solar/reserves/pricing>
    (<verbatim|Fare/Bingo.lean>): all determinants, powers of beta and Haar
    constants. The tag sum is one.

    <item><verbatim|Fare.climbs/wall/crashed> (<verbatim|Fare/Ole.lean>): gap
    in Euclidean fluctuation directions on a coordinate-sup safe chart; chart
    recognition for alive tags; large-wire energy penalty.

    <item><verbatim|Fare.polar/overest/rays> (<verbatim|Fare/Jasper.lean>):
    two-case exterior estimate.

    <item><verbatim|Fare.faceM/outside_est/coolant>
    (<verbatim|Fare/Slate.lean>): uniform fine toll Lipschitz estimate and
    slack witness obtained by contradiction.

    <item><verbatim|Fare.red/market/overdraft/chairs/bench>
    (<verbatim|Fare/Verm.lean>) and <verbatim|Fare.loopbill/classbill/tapping/costQ/colo>
    (<verbatim|Fare/Diap.lean>): exact overhead comparison, fifth-order
    classical remainder and determinant cost.

    <item><verbatim|Pane.enlarged/offset/lower/wealthy>
    (<verbatim|Pane/Limes.lean>): absolute funded sector sum with empty term
    one gives lower bound 2-exp(epsilon).

    <item><verbatim|Sienna.Pigment/pencils> (<verbatim|Sienna/Melange.lean>),
    <verbatim|Sienna.posts/minted/crayon> (<verbatim|Sienna/Palette.lean>),
    <verbatim|Sienna.compass/pressures> (<verbatim|Sienna/Oils.lean>),
    <verbatim|Sienna.courtyard/bulks/cooler> (<verbatim|Sienna/Crone.lean>),
    <verbatim|Sienna.rule_it> (<verbatim|Sienna/Ruling.lean>), and
    <verbatim|Sienna.receiptS/reaches> (<verbatim|Sienna/Canvas.lean>):
    simultaneous purchases, existence of one slack configuration, propagation
    and final integral split.

    <item><verbatim|Fare.fury/slack/gamma/mouthF>
    (<verbatim|Fare/Lush.lean>): spreading from the witness to the full
    fluctuation ball and microscopic coarse neighborhood.
  </itemize-minus>

  Retained conditions: actual incoming Cash/Intake, coefficient bounds and
  classical match on that same path, initial chart estimates and fixed-stage
  purchases. No replacement model, no differentiation of fine flags, no
  theorem that these inputs are available on every funded history is inferred
  here.

  <section|Uniform stationary supplier><label|uniform-stationary-supplier>

  <verbatim|uniform-stationary-chart.tex> traces
  <verbatim|YM.Push.Uniform.Receipt> and <verbatim|Receipt.snaps/priced_inverse/adjusted/throughout>
  in <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/STATIONARY_UNIFORM/ImplicitRadius.lean>; the
  localized slope and Hessian differences in <verbatim|Slope.lean>;
  <verbatim|Before.receipt/full_pack/graph> in <verbatim|Paths.lean>; and
  <verbatim|Before.Service.trail_lipschitz> in <verbatim|Along.lean>. Its
  auxiliary-volume polynomial derivative variant uses the same differentiated
  stationarity equation as <verbatim|Response.inverse_feedback/envelopes>,
  but drops higher-order spatial weights after the uniform branch/radius is
  established. It does not claim those discarded weighted response
  conclusions. The final bound is the interface consumed by
  <verbatim|Lapis.illuminates> in <verbatim|Lapis/Quarry.lean>, with
  <verbatim|Lapis.{trench,luminous,patented,wakes}> in
  <verbatim|Lapis/Caverns.lean> and <verbatim|Lapis.pen> in
  <verbatim|Lapis/Misty.lean>. <verbatim|YM.Planned.JetPort.Counter.service>
  in <verbatim|Lean/YM/Planned/STATIONARY_JET_PORT/InUse.lean> is the
  inspected stronger source interface. The exponent price remains affine in
  the loop budget.

  <verbatim|stationary-action-prices.tex> supplies the local-action bound
  from <verbatim|YM.Push.Uniform.{piece,pay_atom,ell_beacon,atom_beacon,pay_support}>
  in <verbatim|Entries.lean>; <verbatim|price_relative/scatter> and
  derivative-series passage in <verbatim|Scatter.lean>;
  <verbatim|named_cost/main_beacons/penalized/paid_ball> in
  <verbatim|ScoreBounds.lean>; <verbatim|frame_comparison/uses_bond/picked_tags/prediction_pay>
  in <verbatim|Prediction.lean>; and finite-read identities in
  <verbatim|Support.lean>. All these files lie under
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/STATIONARY_UNIFORM/>. The already-drafted
  predictor-branch and mean-action-jets arguments supply finite-read
  uniformization of the fixed-patch smooth branch. This does not establish
  any new pre-block quantitative price or improve history widths.

  <section|Evidence and remaining checks><label|evidence-and-remaining-checks>

  The listed source files were read with <verbatim|cat>, <verbatim|sed>, and
  bounded <verbatim|rg> searches on 2026-11-12. No Lean source was edited,
  and no Lean build or axiom replay was run in this pass. The shared
  literature directory was checked; the additional arguments are
  finite-dimensional calculus, exact change of variables and explicit
  inequalities. No new external theorem match is asserted.

  At 04:24 UTC, <verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> passed for the
  then-integrated unit files. The corresponding LaTeX build completed (503
  pages); four overflow warnings were isolated to the Crown section and its
  displayed equations were subsequently reformatted. A clean rebuild and
  visual checks follow integration.

